      en: "On the bank of the Jadukata at Laurergarh in Tahirpur stands the shrine (astana) of Shah Arefin (R.). According to tradition he was one of the saints who accompanied Hazrat Shah Jalal (R.) and helped spread Islam in this region, and the hilly riverside setting gives the shrine a deeply peaceful air.\n\nHis annual urs in the Bengali month of Chaitra draws hundreds of thousands of devotees from across the country. Around the same time, Hindu pilgrims gather on the same river for the Panatirtha holy bath — a rare meeting of two faiths on one riverbank that speaks to the area’s long tradition of coexistence.\n\nFor the rest of the year the shrine is quiet. It lies within walking distance of Barik Tila and the Jadukata ghat, so it is easy to include in the same day trip.",
