      en: "Hugging the Tripura border in Chunarughat, Habiganj, the Rema-Kalenga Wildlife Sanctuary is one of the largest surviving natural forests in Bangladesh. Made up of the Rema, Kalenga, Chhonbari and Rashidpur beats, it is remote and relatively little visited — which is exactly why it still feels truly wild.\n\nSeveral primate species, barking deer and wild boar live here, along with a bird list reported to exceed three hundred species; locals say rarer animals such as bears and yellow-throated martens still roam the deeper forest. Tripura, Santal and other communities live in villages within the sanctuary, and there is a watchtower and a few walking trails.\n\nAccess roads are rough, so winter (November–February) is by far the best season. For anyone who wants a real forest experience without crowds, this is the ideal offbeat trek.",
