      en: "Deep inside the Rajkandi Reserve Forest of Kamalganj, Moulvibazar, lies Hum Hum waterfall. It reportedly became widely known only around 2010, when a group of travellers brought it to public attention; before that it was known mainly to local indigenous people and forest workers. Local tradition says the name echoes the humming roar of the falls.\n\nGetting there is an adventure in itself: a walk of several hours from Kalabonpara through bamboo groves, along rocky streams and over slippery hillocks under thick jungle. At the end, the water drops down a tall rock face into a cool pool, and the effort is instantly forgotten.\n\nThe falls are fullest from late monsoon into autumn (August–October), though the trail is then muddy and full of leeches. In the dry season the walk is easier but the flow drops sharply.",
