      en: "Inside Hail Haor near Sreemangal, Baikka Beel is a permanent fish and bird sanctuary. It is reported to have been protected around 2003 with the involvement of local communities, and fish and bird numbers have grown significantly since.\n\nFrom the watchtower on the bank you look over water lilies and lotus beds dotted with cormorants, purple swamphens, herons and pheasant-tailed jacanas, joined in winter by large flocks of ducks. It is one of the country’s favourite spots for birders and wildlife photographers, and the wide open views and stillness of the surrounding haor are deeply calming.\n\nDecember to February, especially at dawn, is the best time to visit, when migratory birds are most numerous. Approach roads can be muddy in the monsoon.",
