      en: "About 16 km west of Mymensingh city, Muktagacha is home to the sprawling palace complex of its zamindars. The Acharya Chowdhury family ran one of the most influential estates in greater Mymensingh and were known as patrons of education and culture.\n\nThe complex contains several palaces, temples, the remains of a theatre hall and ponds. Many buildings are now dilapidated, but arches, pillars, carved doors and wall decoration still convey the old grandeur, and parts of the complex have reportedly been taken up for conservation.\n\nMuktagacha is also famous for its monda, a sweet said to have been made here for nearly two centuries and once served at the zamindars’ court. Seeing the rajbari and then tasting monda in the same bazar is an essential part of the trip. Winter is the best time to go.",
