      en: "Lauchapra recreation centre sits in the lap of the Garo hills in Bakshiganj upazila, Jamalpur. Rolling hillocks, sal and mixed forest, and the hills of Meghalaya rising across the border make it a quiet hill retreat in this corner of the north.\n\nThe main attraction is the watchtower on a high hillock, from where the green swells of the Garo hills roll away to the horizon and the Indian border. Walks along the hill paths, a small lake, and glimpses of life in nearby Garo and other indigenous villages are further reasons to come.\n\nNovember to February is the best season, with dry weather and clear skies. Weekends bring picnic groups; weekdays are far more peaceful.",
