      en: "As a boy, national poet Kazi Nazrul Islam spent some time in Trishal, Mymensingh, and studied at Darirampur school. The Nazrul memorial centre built around those memories displays photographs, information panels and mementos from the poet’s life, and the Jatiya Kabi Kazi Nazrul Islam University, named in his honour, stands nearby.\n\nLocal people still tell stories of the young Nazrul — tradition holds that he used to play the flute under a banyan tree here. Darirampur school, the house associated with his stay and that banyan tree together make Trishal a place of pilgrimage for admirers of his poetry and songs.\n\nIt can be visited year-round, but the poet’s birth anniversary in May (the Bengali month of Jaishtha) brings cultural programmes and a fair, when the atmosphere is at its liveliest.",
